From 80a6f9a83e562cbb07e529cbce034ec4f5234f7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 05:20:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ReSTIR: GI path reconnection, 64 B reservoir record, GI pool
 off by default
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

① GI RECONNECTION — Project-Zero ReSTIRSequence.slang + its CPU harness

IndirectReservoirCombine took wB = b.wsum verbatim, so a reused indirect
sample transferred the NEIGHBOUR's throughput — its albedo, its cosines and
its bounce geometry — and the receiver shaded with a path that never
happened at that pixel. DirectReservoirCombine never had this problem: its
target is rebuilt from the receiver's own normal and albedo, because the
thing it stores (Le) is a property of the light both pixels share.

The indirect pool now carries the second-bounce direction (dir2) so the
receiver can RECONNECT the path at its own surface, and the combine scores
the offer against the receiver's own target:

    wB = pB * b.wsum / pBb      pB  = target(receiver's re-traced path)
                                pBb = target(the neighbour's stored path)

If the neighbour wins, the DIRECTION travels; the throughput does not — the
reservoir stores the receiver's reconnected values.

Reconnection alone is not enough: measured, it halved the floor probe's
error but TRIPLED its standard error (0.004021 -> 0.008234; floor-left
0.006001 -> 0.019279), because reconnecting across a bounce that lands on
different geometry swings pB/pBb by orders of magnitude. The standard
companion is a domain restriction — merge only where the receiver's first
bounce hits geometry iff the offer's did. Skipping a merge adds no M and
conditions on nothing about the sample's outcome, so it is not a bias.

    probe          reference    before      reconnect   reconnect+gate
    floor GI       0.184292     0.188477    0.180662    0.185305
    floor-left GI  0.189269     0.184998    0.194289    0.185406
    wall    GI     0.190209     0.187772    0.186970    0.186970
    mean |error|                0.003964    0.003963    0.002705

T4 determinism PASS and all six probes PASS.

② 64 B RESERVOIR RECORD — ViewportIntegrator.slang + SwapchainExchange.cpp

GpuReservoir was 80 B and carried two fields no decision ever consumed:
SelectedUv (8 B, threaded through every merge and publish; PHatFull needs
only toLight, PHatSky only the direction, and Sample.xyz already holds the
point) and Counts.z (Visible, written by every publish, read by nothing).
Dropping both lets W and the view depth move into padding that was already
reserved, so the record is four vec4s: 2 x 265 MB -> 2 x 212 MB across the
ping-pong pair at 1920x1080, and a fifth less reservoir traffic. The host
static_assert moves 80 -> 64 and is the contract with the shader.

③ GI POOL OFF BY DEFAULT — ReSTIRIntegrator.h

kFeatureGiReuse ran a second complete ReSTIR pipeline on ~16 % of surface
pixels for a measured 0.6-1.6 % RMSE gain. Now off; the switch and the
DiagnosticInspector readout stay, so the A/B is one checkbox away. This
also retires the cost of ①, which adds a re-trace per tap.
